1
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:06,830
Thanks for the tasty dinner.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:06,830
You're welcome for a tasty dinner.

3
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:09,040
What are you guys looking at?

4
00:00:09,210 --> 00:00:11,800
Ross and the most beautiful girl in the world.

5
00:00:11,970 --> 00:00:13,420
Yeah, come to Papa!

6
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:20,420
I know!

7
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:24,430
Probably the only time I'll say this...

8
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:26,760
...but did you see the ass on her?

9
00:00:27,610 --> 00:00:29,690
What did you? When did you?

10
00:00:30,110 --> 00:00:32,650
How did you? How did you get a girl like that?

11
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:38,240
So what is she, like a spokesmodel? An aerobics instructor?

12
00:00:38,410 --> 00:00:43,620
Actually, she's a paleontology doctoral candidate...

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,160
...specializing in the Cenozoic Era.

14
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:46,870
But that's, like, the easiest era.

15
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:51,620
I've seen her at work, but I always figured...

16
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:56,210
But, uh, I made her dinner.

17
00:00:56,890 --> 00:01:00,130
We had a great time. And we're going out again tomorrow.

18
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:06,630
Maybe her friends are betting to see who gets the biggest geek.

19
00:01:06,810 --> 00:01:08,640
Fine by me. Hope she wins.

20
00:01:58,160 --> 00:01:59,190
Hey!

21
00:01:59,360 --> 00:02:00,820
You have any wrapping paper?

22
00:02:01,620 --> 00:02:03,200
Is it for my birthday present?

23
00:02:03,870 --> 00:02:06,360
It was your birthday months ago.

24
00:02:06,540 --> 00:02:10,120
You said you ordered something special and it just hadn't come yet.

25
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:15,000
I have a call in about that.

26
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:17,300
Oh. Okay.

27
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:19,710
It's for Kathy. It's an early copy of her favorite book.

28
00:02:22,220 --> 00:02:24,090
Oh! The Velveteen Rabbit!

29
00:02:24,260 --> 00:02:26,880
When the boy's love makes the rabbit real...

30
00:02:27,060 --> 00:02:28,770
Don't touch it, because your fingers have destructive oils.

31
00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:33,890
Then you'd better keep it away from Ross' hair.

32
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:38,940
This is pretty rare. How did you get that?

33
00:02:39,110 --> 00:02:42,980
No big deal. I just went to some bookstores...

34
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:46,580
...talked to some dealers, called some of the author's grandchildren.

35
00:02:47,410 --> 00:02:48,900
Honey, that's so sweet.

36
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:52,120
What a great way to say, "I secretly love you, roommate's girlfriend."

37
00:02:54,630 --> 00:02:57,540
It doesn't say that.

38
00:02:56,750 --> 00:02:57,750
Does it?

39
00:02:58,470 --> 00:03:02,960
How will it look when you get her something incredibly meaningful...

40
00:03:03,140 --> 00:03:05,500
...and expensive, and her boyfriend, Joey, gives her an orange?

41
00:03:07,430 --> 00:03:10,890
I'll make sure Joey gets her something really great.

42
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:12,600
It's got to be better than that book.

43
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:14,720
Ooh! Like a crossbow!

44
00:03:17,610 --> 00:03:19,190
Once again, I am sorry.

45
00:03:19,610 --> 00:03:20,850
Thank you. Bye.

46
00:03:22,450 --> 00:03:26,360
I had to turn down a job catering a funeral for 60 people.

47
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:29,400
Oh, my God! What happened?

48
00:03:29,870 --> 00:03:31,240
Sixty guests.

49
00:03:35,290 --> 00:03:37,120
Why'd you have to turn it down?

50
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:41,460
I don't have the money or equipment...

51
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:43,300
...to handle something that big on such short notice.

52
00:03:43,550 --> 00:03:45,790
Wow, what is with all the negativity?

53
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:48,800
You sound like "Moni-can't," not "Moni-can"!

54
00:03:50,850 --> 00:03:52,090
Moni-ca.

55
00:03:54,190 --> 00:03:57,350
You've been playing around with this catering for years.

56
00:03:57,520 --> 00:04:00,480
Do you want to be a caterer?

57
00:03:57,520 --> 00:04:00,480
I don't know.

58
00:04:00,650 --> 00:04:02,560
There you go! That's the spirit!

59
00:04:03,570 --> 00:04:07,990
If you need money, I will lend you money. Just get moving!

60
00:04:08,370 --> 00:04:11,950
Really? I'd need $500 for all the food and supplies.

61
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:16,710
It's worth it if it'll get you moving. You haven't worked in months!

62
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:18,040
Neither have you.

63
00:04:18,210 --> 00:04:19,620
Yes, but I'm doing this.

64
00:04:21,210 --> 00:04:22,750
That would be great! Thank you.

65
00:04:24,010 --> 00:04:25,970
Hey!

66
00:04:24,010 --> 00:04:25,970
Hey!

67
00:04:28,050 --> 00:04:29,170
Can I borrow your apartment keys?

68
00:04:29,850 --> 00:04:30,880
Why?

69
00:04:34,690 --> 00:04:35,930
You can pee here.

70
00:04:38,520 --> 00:04:43,030
Ha-ha-ha. Yes, I can, of course. Excuse me.

71
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:46,360
It's okay. The duck's using our bathroom anyway.

72
00:04:49,870 --> 00:04:51,950
What are you getting for her birthday?

73
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:54,490
We've been dating a couple weeks. I got to get her something?

74
00:04:54,790 --> 00:04:55,870
Yes!

75
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:59,000
Yes! You have to get her something really nice.

76
00:05:00,090 --> 00:05:04,380
I know!

77
00:05:00,090 --> 00:05:04,380
And not one of your coupons...

78
00:05:02,460 --> 00:05:04,260
...for an hour of "Joey Love."

79
00:05:10,470 --> 00:05:12,460
Ooh! A crossword! Can I help?

80
00:05:11,890 --> 00:05:13,060
No!

81
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:16,340
Last week I got all but three answers...

82
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:18,260
...and I want to finish one without any help.

83
00:05:18,610 --> 00:05:19,590
Fine.

84
00:05:20,070 --> 00:05:22,560
But you can't help me develop my new universal language.

85
00:05:25,570 --> 00:05:26,940
Hey!

86
00:05:25,570 --> 00:05:26,940
How'd it go?

87
00:05:27,110 --> 00:05:29,980
Oh, my God! It was the best funeral ever!

88
00:05:31,030 --> 00:05:32,900
Everyone loved the food.

89
00:05:33,080 --> 00:05:34,820
I even got another funeral for tomorrow.

90
00:05:35,750 --> 00:05:38,080
The dead guy from today's best friend.

91
00:05:38,540 --> 00:05:41,500
It's like I am the official caterer for that accident.

92
00:05:42,420 --> 00:05:44,410
Mon, I'm so happy for you!

93
00:05:44,590 --> 00:05:46,830
Thanks. Check out my new catering stuff.

94
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:49,590
Look! I'm an omelet station!

95
00:05:50,220 --> 00:05:51,630
Omelet? Made to order?

96
00:05:50,220 --> 00:05:51,630
Ha!

97
00:05:53,140 --> 00:05:54,930
I'll have one, please. Plus my money.

98
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:58,020
Oh...

99
00:05:58,100 --> 00:06:00,440
I didn't realize you needed it right away.

100
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:03,510
You told me to go and be a caterer. So I went. I be'd.

101
00:06:05,530 --> 00:06:07,270
I used it to buy all this stuff.

102
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:11,770
I got another job tomorrow, so I'll pay you back then.

103
00:06:11,780 --> 00:06:15,120
Oh! Okay. Sorry I acted like a bank.

104
00:06:25,710 --> 00:06:28,670
Um, would you like to come in?

105
00:06:29,340 --> 00:06:32,510
Did Homo erectus hunt with wooden tools?

106
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:35,970
According to recent findings.

107
00:06:47,820 --> 00:06:49,650
Here, Mitzi! Here, Mitzi!

108
00:06:50,820 --> 00:06:53,660
Uh, Mitzi is?

109
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:55,660
My hamster.

110
00:06:56,490 --> 00:06:58,490
I hope she's okay. I haven't seen her in a while.

111
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:00,610
Have a seat.

112
00:07:01,170 --> 00:07:02,250
Where?

113
00:07:03,580 --> 00:07:05,670
Uh, oh! Do you, uh...?

114
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:13,420
Do you have any, um, Cinnamon Fruit Toasties?

115
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:15,430
What?

116
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:15,430
Well, I do.

117
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:20,600
Let's go back to my place, light a couple candles...

118
00:07:20,770 --> 00:07:23,850
...break open a box of Cinnamon Fruit Toasties?

119
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:27,360
I'd rather not.

120
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:27,360
Oh, yeah? Why not?

121
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:33,030
Okay, um... Don't take this the wrong way...

122
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:36,610
...but your place kind of has a weird smell.

123
00:07:43,830 --> 00:07:46,580
Is everything in the car?

124
00:07:43,830 --> 00:07:46,580
Did you settle the bill?

125
00:07:46,750 --> 00:07:49,040
No. I hate this part.

126
00:07:50,090 --> 00:07:53,010
Ooh! Oh! Look what we almost left!

127
00:07:53,050 --> 00:07:54,040
That's not mine.

128
00:07:53,050 --> 00:07:54,040
Oh.

129
00:07:55,350 --> 00:07:56,760
Ooh. Look what we almost took!

130
00:08:05,190 --> 00:08:06,300
Excuse me, Ms. Burkart?

131
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:08,850
Well, we're all cleaned up.

132
00:08:09,070 --> 00:08:12,530
Oh. Good. Thank you.

133
00:08:14,030 --> 00:08:15,530
Um, ahem...

134
00:08:15,950 --> 00:08:19,610
And, well, there's this small matter of the, um...

135
00:08:20,910 --> 00:08:24,400
Dear?

136
00:08:20,910 --> 00:08:24,400
The matter of...

137
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:25,170
...payment.

138
00:08:26,210 --> 00:08:29,420
Jack used to handle the finances.

139
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:46,090
You know what we should all do?

140
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:46,600
Go see a musical.

141
00:08:49,190 --> 00:08:50,400
Sure.

142
00:08:51,940 --> 00:08:53,650
You know which one?

143
00:08:54,530 --> 00:08:57,490
The 1996 Tony Award winner.

144
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:01,690
Do you know the name of that one?

145
00:09:01,870 --> 00:09:03,830
I don't know, um, Grease?

146
00:09:05,670 --> 00:09:06,700
No.

147
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:09,950
Rent?

148
00:09:10,880 --> 00:09:12,460
Yes! Rent!

149
00:09:13,630 --> 00:09:15,120
So when do you want to go?

150
00:09:15,300 --> 00:09:17,710
What? I'm sorry. I can't, I'm busy.

151
00:09:21,140 --> 00:09:22,220
Hey...

152
00:09:23,140 --> 00:09:25,930
Man, it is so hard to shop for girls. Ugh!

153
00:09:27,650 --> 00:09:29,810
Yes, it is, at Office Max!

154
00:09:32,820 --> 00:09:34,180
What did you get her?

155
00:09:35,650 --> 00:09:36,980
A pen.

156
00:09:38,320 --> 00:09:41,610
It's two gifts in one. It's a pen that's also a clock. Huh?

157
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:46,080
Ha, ha. You can't give her that.

158
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:46,080
Why not?

159
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:48,330
She's not 11!

160
00:09:49,830 --> 00:09:51,500
And it's not the seventh night of Chanukah.

161
00:09:55,170 --> 00:09:59,170
What he means by that is, while this is a very nice gift...

162
00:09:59,340 --> 00:10:01,800
...maybe it's not something a boyfriend gives.

163
00:10:01,970 --> 00:10:03,130
Sure, it is.

164
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:05,010
She needs a pen for work.

165
00:10:05,180 --> 00:10:06,760
She's writing. She turns it over. "Whoa! It's time for my date with Joey!"

166
00:10:11,690 --> 00:10:16,230
All right. What did you get for Angela Del Veccio's birthday?

167
00:10:16,690 --> 00:10:18,690
She didn't have one.

168
00:10:18,860 --> 00:10:19,940
For three years?

169
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:27,570
Look, it's too late, and I got an audition.

170
00:10:26,370 --> 00:10:28,410
I can't shop anymore.

171
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:33,620
I will go out and try to find something for her.

172
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:35,130
Thanks, man.

173
00:10:36,130 --> 00:10:37,870
While you're at it, could you get her a card?

174
00:10:39,220 --> 00:10:41,920
Would you like me to write her a little poem as well?

175
00:10:42,470 --> 00:10:45,210
Or just get a card that has a poem already in it.

176
00:10:48,560 --> 00:10:52,520
Oh! You have to get our money.

177
00:10:48,560 --> 00:10:52,520
She couldn't stop crying.

178
00:10:52,690 --> 00:10:55,230
With those thick glasses, her tears look giant.

179
00:10:56,730 --> 00:10:57,940
I know, it's tough.

180
00:10:58,110 --> 00:11:01,520
You know what the first thing I did after my mom's funeral was?

181
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:03,150
What?

182
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:03,150
Pay the caterer!

183
00:11:04,830 --> 00:11:06,530
I've had a lot of jobs.

184
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:09,750
And there are some people who always try to get out of paying.

185
00:11:10,290 --> 00:11:12,660
It's either "That massage wasn't long enough"...

186
00:11:12,830 --> 00:11:14,570
...or "I don't know any of those songs"...

187
00:11:14,750 --> 00:11:17,960
...or "These sombreros aren't big enough. Bad little white girl!"

188
00:11:20,340 --> 00:11:21,630
Okay.

189
00:11:22,090 --> 00:11:24,080
So you think she's faking?

190
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:27,930
There weren't any tears till you showed her the bill.

191
00:11:28,100 --> 00:11:29,930
She sounded pretty upset to me.

192
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:32,440
You're a grand old flag

193
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:36,730
You're a high     -flying flag And forever in peace may you wave

194
00:11:37,570 --> 00:11:38,900
She seems fine now.

195
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:49,530
So you just left? Her place was really that bad?

196
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:53,120
You throw your jacket on a chair at the end of the day.

197
00:11:53,670 --> 00:11:57,280
Like that, only instead of a chair, it's a pile of garbage.

198
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:02,050
And instead of a jacket, it's a pile of garbage.

199
00:12:03,340 --> 00:12:05,880
And instead of the end of the day, it's the end of time...

200
00:12:06,970 --> 00:12:09,260
...and garbage is all that has survived.

201
00:12:11,810 --> 00:12:13,140
Here.

202
00:12:11,810 --> 00:12:13,140
Wow. Thanks.

203
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:16,350
So, uh, what happened?

204
00:12:16,520 --> 00:12:18,760
Nothing. I had to get out of there.

205
00:12:18,900 --> 00:12:21,320
Next time, you take her to your place.

206
00:12:21,610 --> 00:12:24,320
I tried that. She says it has a weird smell.

207
00:12:25,570 --> 00:12:27,660
What kind of smell?

208
00:12:25,570 --> 00:12:27,660
I don't know. Soap?

209
00:12:29,830 --> 00:12:32,410
Listen, you like this girl, right?

210
00:12:29,830 --> 00:12:32,410
Yeah.

211
00:12:32,580 --> 00:12:33,990
You want to see her again?

212
00:12:32,580 --> 00:12:33,990
Yeah.

213
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:35,780
So you're going to have to do it in the mess!

214
00:12:38,130 --> 00:12:39,790
Yeah, okay. You're right.

215
00:12:41,130 --> 00:12:44,710
I mean, uh, who cares about a little sloppiness?

216
00:12:44,510 --> 00:12:46,180
Yeah.

217
00:12:46,510 --> 00:12:48,850
It's endearing, really.

218
00:12:46,510 --> 00:12:48,850
All right!

219
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:50,970
Now you go get that beautiful pig!

220
00:13:01,940 --> 00:13:05,450
I just spent the entire afternoon looking for a present...

221
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:08,490
...for Kathy that would be better than the rabbit.

222
00:13:08,990 --> 00:13:09,980
Any luck?

223
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:13,690
Yeah, I found this great place called "Invisible Things for Kathy."

224
00:13:14,660 --> 00:13:16,370
Can you give me a hand with all this stuff?

225
00:13:17,920 --> 00:13:21,710
Just return the book, let Joey give her the clock pen...

226
00:13:21,880 --> 00:13:23,960
...and you get her something worse than that...

227
00:13:24,550 --> 00:13:25,710
...like a regular pen.

228
00:13:27,220 --> 00:13:28,830
She's really going to love this, you know?

229
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:32,510
The bottom line is, I want her to have it...

230
00:13:33,390 --> 00:13:36,430
...even if I don't get to be the one who gives it to her.

231
00:13:37,400 --> 00:13:38,890
Aw, honey, that's so sweet.

232
00:13:38,980 --> 00:13:42,230
Yeah? You don't think it's just pathetic?

233
00:13:42,650 --> 00:13:43,860
Oh, "pathetic"!

234
00:13:46,950 --> 00:13:50,490
Hey! I've been looking all over for you.

235
00:13:50,950 --> 00:13:51,940
Where?

236
00:13:50,950 --> 00:13:51,940
Our place. The hall.

237
00:13:57,920 --> 00:13:59,280
I got something.

238
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:07,130
It's a book.

239
00:14:08,890 --> 00:14:09,870
A book?

240
00:14:11,550 --> 00:14:13,590
Is it a book that's also a safe?

241
00:14:16,270 --> 00:14:17,680
It's a book that's just a book.

242
00:14:18,060 --> 00:14:21,900
It's The Velveteen Rabbit. It was her favorite as a kid.

243
00:14:22,520 --> 00:14:25,270
So, uh, just let me know if she likes it, okay?

244
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:28,060
You got it.

245
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:28,610
Thanks for doing this. I owe you one.

246
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:35,490
There wasn't any change from that twenty, was there?

247
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:38,790
No, it came out to an even twenty.

248
00:14:40,830 --> 00:14:43,290
Wow. That's almost as much as a new book.

249
00:14:48,800 --> 00:14:51,090
Jeepers Creepers

250
00:14:51,260 --> 00:14:52,970
Where'd you get those peepers?

251
00:14:53,140 --> 00:14:56,760
Jeepers Creepers Where'd you get those eyes?

252
00:14:57,100 --> 00:14:58,340
You didn't get the money?

253
00:14:58,520 --> 00:15:00,050
Maybe I can try at intermission?

254
00:15:01,730 --> 00:15:03,560
You know what? Let's just go.

255
00:15:03,730 --> 00:15:06,520
No! Hey! We're not leaving till we get paid!

256
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:08,850
I don't know who she thinks she is.

257
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:11,030
Enough is enough!

258
00:15:11,990 --> 00:15:13,070
Hey, widow?

259
00:15:14,830 --> 00:15:15,860
Widow? Excuse me? Excuse me!

260
00:15:20,160 --> 00:15:24,620
Thanks. Um, clearly this is a very, very hard time for you.

261
00:15:24,790 --> 00:15:28,380
Um, but we provided a service, and we deserve to be paid...

262
00:15:28,550 --> 00:15:29,880
...because you ate that service.

263
00:15:30,050 --> 00:15:33,960
We are not leaving here until we are paid every penny, because...

264
00:15:34,140 --> 00:15:37,430
...we're part-time caterers and we have no place else to go.

265
00:15:40,230 --> 00:15:43,430
All right. I'll get my bag.

266
00:15:43,020 --> 00:15:44,060
Good.

267
00:15:52,070 --> 00:15:53,780
I'm going to leave some cards here.

268
00:15:56,410 --> 00:15:58,780
Please think of us for your next event.

269
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:07,740
You want to come inside?

270
00:16:08,550 --> 00:16:09,880
Yes.

271
00:16:11,920 --> 00:16:13,540
Yes, I do.

272
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:25,100
I'll be right back. Make yourself comfortable.

273
00:16:50,340 --> 00:16:52,580
Guess who.

274
00:16:50,340 --> 00:16:52,580
Uh...

275
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:55,710
Department of Sanitation?

276
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:58,760
It's me.

277
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:58,760
Ha, oh!

278
00:17:10,610 --> 00:17:12,480
Aw!

279
00:17:13,440 --> 00:17:14,600
What?

280
00:17:14,780 --> 00:17:15,990
Oh, Cheryl!

281
00:17:14,780 --> 00:17:15,990
Oh, Ross!

282
00:17:18,780 --> 00:17:21,200
Oh! Oh!

283
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:28,830
Oh! God!

284
00:17:30,210 --> 00:17:32,500
Aah! Oh, my God!

285
00:17:36,630 --> 00:17:38,590
No! No!

286
00:17:39,010 --> 00:17:41,390
It's my hamster! It's Mitzi!

287
00:17:41,640 --> 00:17:45,380
Oh, my God! I'm so sorry. I must have freaked out.

288
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:47,300
Thank God it's not Mitzi!

289
00:17:48,020 --> 00:17:49,310
It's just a rat.

290
00:17:53,780 --> 00:17:55,390
I did it! Aah!

291
00:17:55,740 --> 00:17:58,150
I finished it! I did it all by myself!

292
00:17:58,910 --> 00:18:00,400
And there's nobody to hug.

293
00:18:09,290 --> 00:18:11,210
Hey! Hey, you guys!

294
00:18:11,500 --> 00:18:13,630
I finished it all by myself! Hug me.

295
00:18:13,840 --> 00:18:15,420
Yay! So good!

296
00:18:16,420 --> 00:18:17,910
Congratulations.

297
00:18:16,420 --> 00:18:17,910
Thank you.

298
00:18:18,590 --> 00:18:20,830
How did it go?

299
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:23,850
The widow wouldn't pay, so Phoebe yelled at her till she did.

300
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:25,340
I'm a hard-ass.

301
00:18:28,140 --> 00:18:29,260
And I'm a wuss. We should be partners.

302
00:18:31,560 --> 00:18:34,060
Hard-ass and wuss. We could fight crime.

303
00:18:36,610 --> 00:18:40,020
Wait a minute, Phoebe.

304
00:18:38,740 --> 00:18:40,400
We should be partners.

305
00:18:40,700 --> 00:18:42,860
We should be catering partners.

306
00:18:43,030 --> 00:18:46,900
You're not working now, and we have a great time together.

307
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:49,740
Okay.

308
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:49,740
I cook and you take care of the money.

309
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:52,120
Oh! Lt'll be like I have a wife in the '50s!

310
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:58,540
Hey.

311
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:58,540
Hey!

312
00:18:59,050 --> 00:19:00,510
How did she like the gift?

313
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:03,880
She loved it. She's showing the girls right now.

314
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:05,260
Yeah? That's great.

315
00:19:05,430 --> 00:19:09,970
I got to tell you...

316
00:19:06,970 --> 00:19:09,890
...I feel bad taking credit for this, because...

317
00:19:10,140 --> 00:19:12,230
...am I going to get a lot of credit for this!

318
00:19:17,730 --> 00:19:18,780
Hey.

319
00:19:17,730 --> 00:19:18,780
Hey.

320
00:19:18,940 --> 00:19:21,110
Hey. Happy birthday.

321
00:19:21,320 --> 00:19:22,740
Thank you.

322
00:19:22,910 --> 00:19:25,240
You know, uh, Chandler got you a gift too.

323
00:19:26,660 --> 00:19:27,740
No, he didn't.

324
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:32,370
Yeah, he did. Look, it's right there on the counter. Ho, ho!

325
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:43,750
Happy birthday.

326
00:19:42,760 --> 00:19:44,010
I'm sorry.

327
00:19:46,430 --> 00:19:48,010
You really didn't have to.

328
00:19:49,100 --> 00:19:51,270
Wow!

329
00:19:49,100 --> 00:19:51,270
See...

330
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:55,810
You think it's just a pen, but you turn it over and it's also a clock.

331
00:19:56,440 --> 00:19:58,770
Really? No, this is great!

332
00:19:59,530 --> 00:20:01,520
Thank you, Chandler.

333
00:19:59,530 --> 00:20:01,520
Oh. Yeah.

334
00:20:02,820 --> 00:20:04,110
Aw. Heh.

335
00:20:04,570 --> 00:20:05,780
Want to go to bed?

336
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:08,570
I'll be in, in a minute.

337
00:20:12,620 --> 00:20:16,130
Oh, uh... Don't forget your coupon.

338
00:20:22,170 --> 00:20:23,160
Good night.

339
00:20:25,470 --> 00:20:26,800
Um, thank you for the gift.

340
00:20:27,850 --> 00:20:32,640
Oh, uh, I just knew that sometimes when you're writing...

341
00:20:32,850 --> 00:20:35,650
...you don't always know the exact time.

342
00:20:36,730 --> 00:20:40,320
No, I didn't mean the pen. Thank you for the book.

343
00:20:42,190 --> 00:20:44,610
Uh, the book?

344
00:20:43,150 --> 00:20:44,700
The Velveteen Rabbit?

345
00:20:44,990 --> 00:20:47,150
I have a feeling you had something to do with it.

346
00:20:47,990 --> 00:20:49,030
What do you mean?

347
00:20:49,950 --> 00:20:51,410
When Joey gave it to me he said:

348
00:20:51,580 --> 00:20:54,990
"This is because I know you like rabbits, and I know you like cheese."

349
00:20:59,340 --> 00:21:01,170
Thanks. I love it.

350
00:21:01,340 --> 00:21:03,290
I know how hard it must have been for you to find.

351
00:21:05,630 --> 00:21:08,380
In case you missed that, that sound was, "Oh, well."

352
00:21:10,430 --> 00:21:13,920
You must really like Joey to go to all that trouble.

353
00:21:14,100 --> 00:21:15,680
Oh, yeah. He's my...

354
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:21,890
He's my best friend.

355
00:21:24,610 --> 00:21:26,860
Well...

356
00:21:24,610 --> 00:21:26,860
Good night.

357
00:21:36,210 --> 00:21:38,200
Hey, that coupon expires, you know.

358
00:21:50,050 --> 00:21:53,390
Hi, uh, you don't know me. I'm Monica Geller, Ross' sister.

359
00:21:53,600 --> 00:21:56,850
You know, it's too bad that didn't work out.

360
00:21:56,980 --> 00:21:59,220
Anyway, he told me about your apartment.

361
00:21:59,400 --> 00:22:02,230
Well, I couldn't sleep thinking about it.

362
00:22:04,150 --> 00:22:07,230
So, uh, would it be okay if I cleaned it?

363
00:22:09,780 --> 00:22:10,770
No?

